1
00:00:07,823 --> 00:00:12,606
Somebody stayed past the end of a
shift. It waits here, with a name on it.

2
00:00:13,062 --> 00:00:18,913
They said why, in their own words, at
the time — not a week later from memory.

3
00:00:19,366 --> 00:00:25,450
How long it was, and how much of the day
it makes, before anybody agrees to it.

4
00:00:25,904 --> 00:00:29,991
You say yes or no, and the
decision is kept with your name on it.

5
00:00:30,446 --> 00:00:35,967
Saying yes moves the end of that shift
— which is what makes the counted hours

6
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:39,223
change, rather than a
number being typed over.

7
00:00:39,676 --> 00:00:45,618
And what was asked, by whom, and what
was decided stays readable long after

8
00:00:45,618 --> 00:00:47,757
everybody has forgotten it.

9
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:54,808
Next: the rota itself — who is working,
who is off, and who is missing on Thursday.

